       Maps  are  a  generic  data structure for storage of different types of
       data.  They allow sharing of data between  eBPF  kernel  programs,  and
       also between kernel and user‐space applications.

       Each map type has the following attributes:

       •  type

       •  maximum number of elements

       •  key size in bytes

       •  value size in bytes

       The  following wrapper functions demonstrate how various bbppff() commands
       can be used to access the maps.  The functions use the _c_m_d argument  to
       invoke different operations.

       BBPPFF__MMAAPP__CCRREEAATTEE
